{"title":"FIGURE & FORM DUO WORKSHOP","startsAt":"2026-10-25T09:00:00-04:00","endsAt":"2026-10-25T12:00:00-04:00","status":"ACTIVE","type":"PHYSICAL","description":"We will be creating some beautiful artistic sets with Ciara and Kalopsia, some creative and beatiful sets with some of the best creative models in the country. We will be doing duo creative sets with both models to add some unique images to your portfolio.\n\nTo find out more about the studio and workshop you can visit [https://www.productionstudio.ca](https://www.productionstudio.ca)\n\nThis is a [ticketed](https://www.productionstudio.ca/purchase) event, Secure your spot today!\n\n**Who Should Attend?**\nOur workshops at The Production Studio are designed for photographers looking to expand their skills or build their portfolios in a professional setting. Whether you’re a beginner or an experienced shooter, these sessions offer hands-on learning with top-tier talent from leading agencies.\n\nStudio photography can feel intimidating, but our workshops provide a relaxed environment where you can observe, ask questions, and learn by doing. There’s nothing like hands on experience.\n\nWith a variety of styles and themes, each session ensures participants have the opportunity to shoot one-on-one with models, refine their techniques, and connect with fellow photographers and enthusiasts.\n\n**​ What you should bring:**\n\n* A DSLR/Mirrorless camera\n* Fully Charged Battery\n* Freshly Formatted Memory Card(s)\n* General Lenses: 24-70mm, 24-105mm and 70-200mm If you have a macro lens, 50mm or 85mm please bring it along. It really depends on the type of workshop\n* Pocket Wizards (if you have your own, otherwise one will be provided for you)\n* Bring along a list of shots you’d like to achieve or posing ideas. It can help to ensure that you get the perfect image.\n\n**Workshop Details:**\n\n* ​Arrival: Upon arrival, use the intercom to call unit 205 for entry. Please aim to arrive 15 minutes early to settle in before the session begins.\n* Social Interaction: Feel free to connect with the workshop host and fellow photographers. Keep conversations lighthearted and professional to foster a creative and welcoming environment.\n* Photoshoot Session: Each workshop runs for 3 hours, with participants working one-on-one with the model across 4-5 different sets. The goal is to capture a few standout images from each setup that you can proudly showcase on your website and social media.\n* Model Release: A non-commercial model release, signed by the model, will be provided to each photographer. Photos and videos taken during the workshop can be used for personal promotional purposes only, including portfolios, websites, and print media such as postcards.\n* Please note that behind-the-scenes (BTS) content may be captured by individuals, the model, MUA, or the event host. If you prefer not to be recorded, kindly inform everyone before the event begins.\n\n**Cancellation Policy**\nCancellations are accepted 7-14 days before the workshop (depending on the event) for a full refund. This policy ensures workshops can run smoothly for the studio, models, and MUAs.\n\nThink of workshop registration like purchasing a concert ticket, refunds aren’t typically given. However, if you cancel within 7 days and a replacement is found, a full refund will be issued.\n\nIf the organizer cancels, you’ll receive a full refund. In rare cases, a model may be replaced due to illness, but only with someone of similar look and talent.\n\n**About the organizer:**\nEmanuel Pires has been a photographer for over a decade, leading more than 800 workshops. With years of experience, he offers professional, engaging, and educational sessions designed to inspire creativity. His goal is to build a vibrant community of artists, models, and makeup artists within his professional space.\n\n​To learn more about Emanuel, visit his website [Pires Photography](https://www.piresphotography.ca).\n\nThis is a [ticketed](https://www.productionstudio.ca/purchase) event, Secure your spot today!","venue":{"name":"142 Cawthra Ave","address":"142 Cawthra Ave, Toronto","lat":43.671234,"lng":-79.46491,"city":"Toronto"},"fee":{"amount":200,"currency":"CAD"},"group":"Advance Photographic Workshops","image":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/3/1/6/3/highres_536052643.jpeg"}